IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fraud-nouns`

-- Fraud Act 2006 (2006 c. 35), sections 12 and 13: SUPPLEMENTARY.
--
-- Section 12 makes a company officer guilty too, when the company's offence was committed with
-- the officer's consent or connivance.  Section 13 takes away the privilege against
-- self-incrimination in proceedings relating to property, and gives in exchange an immunity: what
-- is said there cannot be used in evidence against the person (or the spouse or civil partner) in
-- a prosecution for an offence under the Act or a related offence.
--
-- Where section 13 says nothing (proceedings that do not relate to property, an offence of
-- another kind), the answer is the named value "section 13(1) does not apply" / "section 13(2)
-- does not apply": the Act's silence, not a refusal and not a permission.

§ `Supplementary (sections 12 and 13)`

§§ `Section 12: liability of company officers for offences by company`

-- src:111 | 12 Liability of company officers for offences by company
-- src:112 | (1) Subsection (2) applies if an offence under this Act is committed by a body corporate.
-- src:113 | (2) If the offence is proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of—
-- src:114 | (a) a director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body corporate, or
-- src:115 | (b) a person who was purporting to act in any such capacity,
-- src:116 | he (as well as the body corporate) is guilty of the offence and liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.
-- src:117 | (3) If the affairs of a body corporate are managed by its members, subsection (2) applies in relation to the acts and defaults of a member in connection with his functions of management as if he were a director of the body corporate.
@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 12(1), (2), (3) (src:112-117)
GIVEN `the case` IS AN `Officer case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 12(2): the person is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate` `the case` MEANS
    -- (1) an offence under this Act is committed by a body corporate; (2) it is proved that it was
    -- committed with the consent or connivance of a director, manager, secretary or other similar
    -- officer, or a person purporting to act in such a capacity; (3) where the affairs of the body
    -- corporate are managed by its members, a member counts as a director in relation to his
    -- acts and defaults in connection with his functions of management.
    -- "Proved" is a fact the person is asked about (fork F14): the module does not decide proof.
        `the case`'s `an offence under this Act is committed by a body corporate`
    AND (   `the case`'s `it is proved that the offence was committed with the person's consent`
         OR `the case`'s `it is proved that the offence was committed with the person's connivance`)
    AND `section 12(2) and (3): the person is a director, manager, secretary or similar officer, or counts as one` `the case`

@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 12(2)(a), (b), (3) (src:114-115) (src:117)
GIVEN `the case` IS AN `Officer case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 12(2) and (3): the person is a director, manager, secretary or similar officer, or counts as one` `the case` MEANS
        `the case`'s `the person's capacity` EQUALS `a director`
    OR  `the case`'s `the person's capacity` EQUALS `a manager`
    OR  `the case`'s `the person's capacity` EQUALS `a secretary`
    OR  `the case`'s `the person's capacity` EQUALS `another similar officer`
    OR  `the case`'s `the person's capacity` EQUALS `a person purporting to act in any such capacity`
    OR  (    `the case`'s `the person's capacity` EQUALS `a member of a body corporate whose affairs are managed by its members`
         AND `the case`'s `the acts and defaults are in connection with his functions of management`)

§§ `Section 13: evidence`

-- src:118 | 13 Evidence
-- src:119 | (1) A person is not to be excused from—
-- src:120 | (a) answering any question put to him in proceedings relating to property, or
-- src:121 | (b) complying with any order made in proceedings relating to property,
-- src:122 | on the ground that doing so may incriminate him or his spouse or civil partner of an offence under this Act or a related offence.
-- src:123 | (2) But, in proceedings for an offence under this Act or a related offence, a statement or admission made by the person in—
-- src:124 | (a) answering such a question, or
-- src:125 | (b) complying with such an order,
-- src:126 | is not admissible in evidence against him or (unless they married or became civil partners after the making of the statement or admission) his spouse or civil partner.
-- src:127 | (3) “Proceedings relating to property” means any proceedings for—
-- src:128 | (a) the recovery or administration of any property,
-- src:129 | (b) the execution of a trust, or
-- src:130 | (c) an account of any property or dealings with property,
-- src:131 | and “property” means money or other property whether real or personal (including things in action and other intangible property).
-- src:132 | (4) “Related offence” means—
-- src:133 | (a) conspiracy to defraud;
-- src:134 | (b) any other offence involving any form of fraudulent conduct or purpose.
@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 13(3) (src:127-130)
GIVEN `the kind of proceedings` IS A `Kind of proceedings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 13(3): the proceedings are proceedings relating to property` `the kind of proceedings` MEANS
    -- Any proceedings for (a) the recovery or administration of any property, (b) the execution of a
    -- trust, or (c) an account of any property or dealings with property.
        `the kind of proceedings` EQUALS `proceedings for the recovery or administration of any property`
    OR  `the kind of proceedings` EQUALS `proceedings for the execution of a trust`
    OR  `the kind of proceedings` EQUALS `proceedings for an account of any property or dealings with property`

@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 13(4) (src:132-134)
GIVEN `the kind of offence` IS A `Kind of offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 13(4): the offence is a related offence` `the kind of offence` MEANS
    -- (a) conspiracy to defraud; (b) any other offence involving any form of fraudulent conduct or
    -- purpose.  Whether another offence involves fraudulent conduct or purpose is not defined: the
    -- person states it as a fact (fork F16).
        `the kind of offence` EQUALS `conspiracy to defraud`
    OR  `the kind of offence` EQUALS `any other offence involving any form of fraudulent conduct or purpose`

@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 13(1), (2), (4) (src:122) (src:126) (src:132-134)
GIVEN `the kind of offence` IS A `Kind of offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 13(1) and (2): the offence is an offence under this Act or a related offence` `the kind of offence` MEANS
        `the kind of offence` EQUALS `an offence under this Act`
    OR  `section 13(4): the offence is a related offence` `the kind of offence`

@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 13(1) (src:119-122)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Question or order case`
GIVETH AN `Answer under section 13(1)`
`section 13(1): whether the person is excused on the ground of self-incrimination` `the case` MEANS
    -- Applies only to a question put, or an order made, in proceedings relating to property, where
    -- the ground is that doing so may incriminate the person or the person's spouse or civil
    -- partner of an offence under this Act or a related offence.  Anything else is outside what the
    -- section says (fork F15); the Act's silence is named, not guessed.
    IF       `section 13(3): the proceedings are proceedings relating to property` (`the case`'s `the proceedings are`)
         AND NOT (`the case`'s `what is required of the person` EQUALS `neither`)
         AND NOT (`the case`'s `the ground is that doing so may incriminate` EQUALS `neither of them`)
         AND `section 13(1) and (2): the offence is an offence under this Act or a related offence` (`the case`'s `of an offence of the kind`)
    THEN `not excused on that ground`
    ELSE `section 13(1) does not apply`

@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 13(2) (src:123-126)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Statement case`
GIVETH AN `Answer under section 13(2)`
`section 13(2): whether the statement or admission is admissible in evidence` `the case` MEANS
    -- Not admissible against him, or against his spouse or civil partner (unless they married or
    -- became civil partners after the statement or admission was made), in proceedings for an offence
    -- under this Act or a related offence.
    IF       `the case`'s `made in answering such a question or complying with such an order`
         AND `section 13(1) and (2): the offence is an offence under this Act or a related offence` (`the case`'s `the proceedings in which it is to be used are for an offence of the kind`)
         AND (    `the case`'s `it is to be used against` EQUALS `the person who made it`
              OR (    `the case`'s `it is to be used against` EQUALS `the spouse or civil partner of the person who made it`
                  AND NOT (`the case`'s `they married or became civil partners after the making of the statement or admission`)))
    THEN `not admissible in evidence`
    ELSE `section 13(2) does not apply`
